> I dont see how going up and down the stairs without the amulet then
> going back up with the amulet will help your chances of not being sent
> down levels. I'd say youre just lucky.

He can only get the adjacent pets up the stairs, so if all the pets are
not adjacent, he needs to go back down to get the rest of the pets up.
And every time he climbs stairs up in Gehennom, there is the risk that he
doesn't actually get UP the stairs, but is sent down instead.
Dropping the amulet eliminates that risk, so he can get be sure to get the
bunch of pets up before going back down for the next bunch.
So, the only times he may get sent down is when he climbs up with the
amulet, and if I understood correctly, by that time his pets are already
all on the level above.

Compared to just taking the pets he can take with one climbing of the
stairs and leaving the rest behind, it probably doesn't really cut down
the times sent back down, but at least he doesn't need to get all those
pets back up so many times when it happens. 
OTOH, it may increase the time not spent on the same level as some of
the pets, so it may also increase the risk of those pets getting feral.

